# Softlock probe — f3 R5 "Kiln Vault" (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN M5).
#
# This crate *can* be jammed for good: pushed into the bottom-right corner it has a wall on
# the two sides a shove would have to come from, and the silver key on its pit island is then
# unreachable. Leaving the room and coming back rebuilds it on its map cell (01 §9), which is
# what keeps the floor from softlocking.

floor f3
room R5
at 5,6
start hp=6 treasure=0 deaths=0

assert room=R5 silverKeys=0

say Jam: five shoves east and one south, into the corner nothing can reach
push R 5
goto 11,5
push D 1

say Out through d4 and back: the crate is rebuilt on (6,6)
door d4
door d4
assert room=R5 silverKeys=0

say Two shoves north — the second is swallowed by the pit, which stays bridged
goto 6,7
push U 2
goto 6,3
assert room=R5 silverKeys=1
